# Project Structure

## Component Organization

- Each component in its own folder: `src/components/ComponentName/ComponentName.tsx`
- One component per file - no nested component definitions
- Export components from `src/components/index.ts`

## File Structure

```
src/
├── components/      # React components (each in subfolder)
├── hooks/           # Custom hooks
├── lib/             # Constants and utilities
├── types/           # TypeScript interfaces
└── App.tsx          # Main app component
```

## Constants (`lib/constants.ts`)

- Move ALL literal values (strings, arrays, objects) to `lib/constants.ts`
- Add JSDoc comment for each constant explaining its purpose
- Use SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE for constants

## Types (`types/index.ts`)

- Define ALL interfaces in `types/index.ts`
- NO inline type definitions in components
- Props interfaces: `ComponentNameProps`
- Hook returns: `UseHookNameReturn`

## Custom Hooks (`hooks/`)

- Extract reusable logic into custom hooks
- Name hooks with `use` prefix: `useScroll`, `useSlider`
- Export from `hooks/index.ts`

# Performance Patterns

## Always Apply

- Wrap components with `React.memo()`
- Add `displayName` to memoized components
- Use `useMemo` for computed values and rendered arrays
- Use `useCallback` for event handlers and functions passed as props
- Use `React.lazy()` + `Suspense` for below-the-fold components

## Example

```tsx
import { memo, useMemo, useCallback } from "react";

export const Component = memo(function Component({ items }: Props): JSX.Element {
  const renderedItems = useMemo(() => items.map(...), [items]);
  const handleClick = useCallback(() => {...}, []);
  return <div>{renderedItems}</div>;
});

Component.displayName = "Component";
```

# Styling

- Use Tailwind CSS utility classes
- Use `Container` component for consistent layout (48px padding, max-width 1400px)
- Inline styles only when Tailwind classes don't apply correctly
